{
    "_comment_1": "------------------------------------------------------------",
    "_comment_2": "FetchLog Database Configuration",
    "_comment_3": "------------------------------------------------------------",
    "_comment_4": "db_type: which database backend to use for LOG STORAGE.",
    "_comment_5": "  'sqlite'      - local file-based database (default, no setup needed)",
    "_comment_6": "  'postgresql'  - remote PostgreSQL server",
    "_comment_7": "",
    "_comment_8": "When db_type is 'sqlite', only sqlite_path is used.",
    "_comment_9": "When db_type is 'postgresql', the host/port/dbname/user/password/schema",
    "_comment_10": "  fields are used and sqlite_path is ignored.",
    "_comment_11": "",
    "_comment_12": "schema: the PostgreSQL schema to create LOG tables in (default: fetchlog).",
    "_comment_13": "  The schema is created automatically if it does not exist.",
    "_comment_14": "  All tables, indexes, etc. are created on first startup.",
    "_comment_15": "------------------------------------------------------------",

    "db_type": "sqlite",

    "sqlite_path": "logs.db",

    "host": "localhost",
    "port": 5432,
    "dbname": "fetchlog",
    "user": "fetchlog",
    "password": "your_password_here",
    "schema": "fetchlog",

    "_terminal_comment_1": "------------------------------------------------------------",
    "_terminal_comment_2": "Terminal live view - connect with any SSH or telnet client for an",
    "_terminal_comment_3": "  htop-style full-color live log stream (newest entries on top).",
    "_terminal_comment_4": "ssh_port: omit for the default = web port + 1 (e.g. web 5200 ->",
    "_terminal_comment_5": "  SSH 5201); set a port to pin it, or 0 to disable. It needs its",
    "_terminal_comment_6": "  own dedicated port - it cannot share the web port. Under gunicorn",
    "_terminal_comment_7": "  the web port isn't knowable, so set ssh_port here explicitly.",
    "_terminal_comment_8": "telnet_port: 0 (or omit) disables; telnet is OFF by default.",
    "_terminal_comment_9": "The SSH server is embedded in FetchLog (no system sshd needed); its",
    "_terminal_comment_10": "  host key is generated on first start at ssh_host_key.",
    "_terminal_comment_11": "Terminal connections are ALWAYS unauthenticated (read-only view),",
    "_terminal_comment_12": "  even when web auth below is enabled - any client connects with no",
    "_terminal_comment_13": "  credentials. Telnet is also unencrypted - trusted networks only.",
    "_terminal_comment_14": "------------------------------------------------------------",
    "terminal": {
        "telnet_port": 0,
        "ssh_host_key": "ssh_host_key"
    },

    "_auth_comment_1": "------------------------------------------------------------",
    "_auth_comment_2": "Authentication - shared single-sign-on with Leash / 321Theater",
    "_auth_comment_3": "------------------------------------------------------------",
    "_auth_comment_4": "The 'shared' schema (users + app_sessions) lives in the SAME PostgreSQL",
    "_auth_comment_5": "  database the apps run in - it is just a separate schema. So the auth",
    "_auth_comment_6": "  connection is INHERITED from the top-level host/port/dbname/user/password",
    "_auth_comment_7": "  above; you normally only set 'enabled' and 'shared_schema' here. Put",
    "_auth_comment_8": "  connection fields inside this block only to override (shared schema in a",
    "_auth_comment_9": "  different database).",
    "_auth_comment_10": "Auth ALWAYS uses PostgreSQL even when db_type above is 'sqlite', so fill in",
    "_auth_comment_11": "  the top-level host/port/dbname/user/password to reach the shared database.",
    "_auth_comment_12": "Sessions live in <shared_schema>.app_sessions (opaque cookie id); users are",
    "_auth_comment_13": "  read READ-ONLY from <shared_schema>.users (owned by 321Theater). Login is",
    "_auth_comment_14": "  gated on a per-user flag: require_flag = 'is_app_user' (default) or",
    "_auth_comment_15": "  'is_app_admin' (the other flag is still read and kept in the session).",
    "_auth_comment_16": "cookie_name/cookie_domain must match the sibling apps so the browser sends",
    "_auth_comment_17": "  the same cookie to all of them (one host, or a shared parent domain like",
    "_auth_comment_18": "  '.example.com'). Set enabled=false to disable the login gate (dev only).",
    "_auth_comment_19": "------------------------------------------------------------",
    "auth": {
        "enabled": true,
        "shared_schema": "shared",
        "require_flag": "is_app_user",
        "cookie_name": "session",
        "cookie_domain": null,
        "cookie_secure": false,
        "cookie_samesite": "lax",
        "session_lifetime_hours": 12
    }
}
